{"name":"Coffee Gelato","hex":"#bf9779","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"coffee","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A beverage made by infusing the beans of the coffee plant in hot water. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","A serving of this beverage."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a pale brown colour, like that of milk coffee.","Of a table: a small, low table suitable for people in lounge seating to put coffee cups on."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/coffee"},{"term":"gelato","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An Italian variant of ice cream made from milk and sugar, combined with other flavourings. The ingredients are supercooled while stirring to break up ice crystals as they form."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/gelato"}],"entries":[{"title":"Coffee","blocks":[{"text":"Coffee is a beverage brewed from roasted, ground coffee beans. Dark-colored and bitter, coffee has a stimulating effect on humans due to its caffeine content; however decaffeinated coffee is also commercially available. There are also various coffee substitutes."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e4/Latte_and_dark_coffee.jpg/330px-Latte_and_dark_coffee.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Coffee"},{"title":"Gelato","blocks":[{"text":"Gelato refers to a specific type of ice cream of Italian origin. In Italian, gelato is the common word for all types of ice cream. Artisanal gelato in Italy generally contains 6–9% butterfat, which is lower than other styles of frozen dessert. Gelato typically contains 20–35% air, and more flavoring than other types of frozen desserts, giving it an intense flavor with creamy, smooth texture, density and richness that distinguishes it from other ice creams."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3a/Delicious_Gelato_on_display.jpg/330px-Delicious_Gelato_on_display.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gelato"},{"title":"Coffee (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Coffee is a brownish color that is a representation of a roasted coffee bean. Different types of coffee beans have different colors when roasted—the color coffee represents an average."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c5/Roasted_coffee_beans.jpg/330px-Roasted_coffee_beans.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Coffee_(color)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/19/Coffee_beans_unroasted.jpg/500px-Coffee_beans_unroasted.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/19/Coffee_beans_unroasted.jpg/1280px-Coffee_beans_unroasted.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/19/Coffee_beans_unroasted.jpg/500px-Coffee_beans_unroasted.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Green coffee describes the beans before roasting.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACoffee_beans_unroasted.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/60/The_Vertue_of_the_COFFEE_Drink.jpg/330px-The_Vertue_of_the_COFFEE_Drink.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/60/The_Vertue_of_the_COFFEE_Drink.jpg/330px-The_Vertue_of_the_COFFEE_Drink.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A 1652 handbill advertising coffee for sale in St. Michael's Alley, London","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AThe_Vertue_of_the_COFFEE_Drink.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia